# What stays in the repository and never goes into the ZIP of the plugin (tools/build-zip.mjs reads this file).
#
# One pattern per line, the rules of a .gitignore without negation:
#   - a pattern without a slash (`*.zip`, `.*`) matches a name at any depth;
#   - a pattern with a slash (`/tests`, `blocks/src`) is relative to this folder;
#   - `*` stays inside one name, `**` crosses folders; a matched folder is left out with everything in it.
#
# The ZIP holds: casazen.php, uninstall.php, includes/, blocks/build/, languages/, readme.txt and license.txt.

# Dotfiles: .distignore, .gitignore, .wp-env.json, .phpunit.result.cache, ...
.*

# Sources and the tools that are not part of the plugin
/blocks/src
/tests
/tools

# What the build tools install or write
/node_modules
/vendor
/dist
/build
*.zip
*.log

# Package and configuration files of the development tools
/package*.json
/composer.*
/phpcs.xml.dist
/phpunit.xml.dist

# The guide for GitHub readers; the guide inside WordPress is readme.txt
/README.md
